7 8.94641 10.0007 9.4987C10.0007 10.051 10.4484 10.4987 11.0007 10.4987Z"></path><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M5.00065 1.33203H6.33398V1.9987H9.66732V1.33203H11.0007V1.9987H14.6673V13.9987H1.33398V1.9987H5.00065V1.33203ZM5.00065 3.33203H2.66732V12.6654H13.334V3.33203H11.0007V3.9987H9.66732V3.33203H6.33398V3.9987H5.00065V3.33203Z"></path></svg><time dateTime="2026-10-02T17:00:00Z">Friday, October 2-Saturday, October 3  •  1 PM-6 PM</time></div></div></div><div class="SectionWrapper-module-scss-module__5yIgma__section" data-testid="section-wrapper-overview"><div class="Overview-module-scss-module__dJyb9a__title">Overview</div><div class="Overview-module-scss-module__dJyb9a__summaryWrapper"><div class="Overview-module-scss-module__dJyb9a__summary"><p>October 2-3rd, 2026 at Yale University</p><div class="Overview-module-scss-module__dJyb9a__summary"><p><strong><strong>The 83rd Annual English Institute meeting, "Reversal," will take place October 2-3, 2026 at Yale University. This event is co-sponsored by the Whitney Humanities Center.</strong></strong></p><p>For more than seven decades, The English Institute has been a major resource for developments in criticism, theory, and scholarship, while honoring traditional fields of interest and modes of literary analysis.</p><p>Three institutions will now host The English Institute conference: Yale University (2015, 2018, 2023, and 2026), the University of Chicago (2016, 2019, 2024), and the University of California at Irvine (2017, 2022, and 2025).</p><p><strong><strong>Shared reading for "The Conversation": Friedrich Nietzsche, "On Truth and Lying in a Non-Moral Sense" (</strong></strong><a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-uyPEl4uvHumCePUWbGiAMyZP9UmE9Mh/view?usp=drive_link" title="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-uyPEl4uvHumCePUWbGiAMyZP9UmE9Mh/view?usp=drive_link" data-msys-clicktrack="0" target="_blank" rel="ugc nofollow noopener noreferrer"><strong><strong>linked here</strong></strong></a><strong><strong>).</strong></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Schedule</strong></strong></p><p><strong><strong>Friday, October 2</strong></strong></p><p><strong><strong>1:00 pm</strong></strong>: Welcome</p><p><strong><strong>1:10 pm</strong></strong>: Welcome (Yoon Sun Lee and Daniel Stout)</p><p><strong><strong>1:20 pm</strong></strong>: Bonnie Honig, “The Accidental Ordinary: Euripides' <em><em>Hippolytus</em></em> in Reverse” (Introduced by Jennifer Fleissner)</p><p><strong><strong>2:50 pm</strong></strong>: Coffee break</p><p><strong><strong>3:00 pm</strong></strong>: Sarah Beckwith, “The Impossibility of Reversal: Shakespeare’s Turnings in <em><em>The Winter’s Tale</em></em> and Some Intertexts” (Introduced by Nancy Yousef)</p><p><strong><strong>4:30 pm</strong></strong>: Coffee break</p><p><strong><strong>5:00 pm</strong></strong>: Emily Greenwood, “Third Person Regret: Shipwreck and Black Atlantic Counterfactuals” (Introduced by Kevin Quashie)</p><p><strong><strong>6:30 pm:</strong></strong> Opening Reception</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Saturday, October 3</strong></strong></p><p><strong><strong>8:30 am</strong></strong>: Continental breakfast</p><p><strong><strong>9:00 am</strong></strong>: Heather Love, “Doubling Back” (Introduced by Caleb Smith)</p><p><strong><strong>10:45 am</strong></strong>: Coffee break</p><p><strong><strong>11:00am</strong></strong>: Daniel Hack, “Expectations? Great!” (Introduced by Virginia Jackson)</p><p><strong><strong>12:45 pm</strong></strong>: Lunch</p><p><strong><strong>1:45 pm</strong></strong>: The Conversation: Friedrich Nietzsche, “On Truth and Lying in a Non-Moral Sense”</p><p><strong><strong>2:45 pm</strong></strong>: Coffee break</p><p><strong><strong>3:00 pm</strong></strong>: Minou Arjomand, “Aesthetic Labor from Wagner to Abortion Theater” (Introduced by Shonni Enelow)</p><p><strong><strong>4:45 pm</strong></strong>: Mel Y. Chen, “Method’s Negative Spaces” (Introduced by Meredith Martin)</p><p><strong><strong>6:15 pm</strong></strong>: Closing reception</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Travel</strong></strong></p><p>Depending on where you are coming from, there are several ways to travel into New Haven.</p><p><br></p><h3>Air</h3><p><a href="https://www.aveloair.com/" title="https://www.aveloair.com/" data-msys-clicktrack="0" target="_blank" rel="ugc nofollow noopener noreferrer">Avelo Airlines</a> flies to Tweed New Haven Airport (HVN) from twenty-six locations. Yale campus is a 10-15 minute car ride from the airport.</p><p>Please note that most major (New York area) airports are between two and five hours from New Haven via shuttle bus, train, or car. It is best to plan to arrive at these airports in the early morning to early afternoon.</p><p>If you will be flying, we recommend flying into La Guardia International Airport. From there you will take a shuttle bus to Grand Central Station and take the Metro North to New Haven's Union Station. The Metro North runs regularly and does not require purchasing tickets before arriving at the train station. Another excellent option is flying into Newark airport. From Newark you can take an Amtrak train to New Haven's Union Station. While Amtrak prices fluctuate you are able to book in advance and reserve seats.</p><p><br></p><h3>Ground</h3><p>If you are travelling regionally and would like to take the train to New Haven you can take the Metro North from New York City's Grand Central Station to New Haven's Union Station or the Amtrak can be taken from most major hubs to New Haven's Union Station.</p><p>The <a href="https://your.yale.edu/campus-essentials/getting-around-campus/using-the-shuttle" title="https://your.yale.edu/campus-essentials/getting-around-campus/using-the-shuttle" data-msys-clicktrack="0" target="_blank" rel="ugc nofollow noopener noreferrer">Yale Shuttle</a> provides service between Union Station and campus destinations. Please note that there are now TWO shuttle stop locations in front of Union Station. If the stop directly in front of the station is congested, shuttle drivers pick up in front of the parking garage. Please look for Shuttles in both locations.</p><p>Taxis meet all trains and buses at Union Station in New Haven. Include a tip for taxi drivers of about 15% of the total fare; add an extra $1 to $2 for help with luggage. Uber and Lyft are also widely available in New Haven.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Hotels near the conference include</strong></strong></p><p>The Study at Yale</p><p>1157 Chapel Street</p><p>New Haven, CT 06511</p><p>Phone: 203.503.3900</p><p>Estimated price/night: $250-$300</p><p>Website: <a href="https://www.thestudyatyale.com/" title="https://www.thestudyatyale.com/" data-msys-clicktrack="0" target="_blank" rel="ugc nofollow noopener noreferrer">https://www.thestudyatyale.com/</a></p><p><br></p><p>New Haven Hotel</p><p>229 George Street</p><p>New Haven, CT 06510</p><p>Phone: 203-498-3100</p><p>Estimated price/night: $174-$274</p><p>Website: <a href="https://www.newhavenhotel.com/?gad_source=1&amp;gclid=Cj0KCQiAoeGuBhCBARIsAGfKY7zHF28iwfAr8B3Ma6UAPlSZDHwJhcyFZrp666sFXXsa5gbYq3na_oUaAk1QEALw_wcB" title="https://www.newhavenhotel.com/?gad_source=1&amp;gclid=Cj0KCQiAoeGuBhCBARIsAGfKY7zHF28iwfAr8B3Ma6UAPlSZDHwJhcyFZrp666sFXXsa5gbYq3na_oUaAk1QEALw_wcB" data-msys-clicktrack="0" target="_blank" rel="ugc nofollow noopener noreferrer">https://www.newhavenhotel.com/?gad_source=1&amp;gclid=Cj0KCQiAoeGuBhCBARIsAGfKY7zHF28iwfAr8B3Ma6UAPlSZDHwJhcyFZrp666sFXXsa5gbYq3na_oUaAk1QEALw_wcB</a></p><p><br></p><p>OMNI New Haven at Yale</p><p>155 Temple Street</p><p>New Haven, CT 06510</p><p>Phone: 203-772-6664</p><p>Estimated price/night: $150-$250</p><p>Website: <a href="https://www.omnihotels.com/hotels/new-haven-yale?_gl=1*a6pt1v*_gcl_au*MTE3ODYzNzg2MS4xNzc4NTM3MzIz*_ga*MTU4MjYzNjM1MC4xNzc4NTM3MzI0*_ga_BELGX2HEXN*czE3Nzg1MzczMjMkbzEkZzEkdDE3Nzg1MzgxMTAkajI2JGwwJGgw" title="https://www.omnihotels.com/hotels/new-haven-yale?_gl=1*a6pt1v*_gcl_au*MTE3ODYzNzg2MS4xNzc4NTM3MzIz*_ga*MTU4MjYzNjM1MC4xNzc4NTM3MzI0*_ga_BELGX2HEXN*czE3Nzg1MzczMjMkbzEkZzEkdDE3Nzg1MzgxMTAkajI2JGwwJGgw" data-msys-clicktrack="0" target="_blank" rel="ugc nofollow noopener noreferrer">https://www.omnihotels.com/hotels/new-haven-yale?_gl=1*a6pt1v*_gcl_au*MTE3ODYzNzg2MS4xNzc4NTM3MzIz*_ga*MTU4MjYzNjM1MC4xNzc4NTM3MzI0*_ga_BELGX2HEXN*czE3Nzg1MzczMjMkbzEkZzEkdDE3Nzg1MzgxMTAkajI2JGwwJGgw</a></p><p><br></p><p>The Graduate by Hilton New Haven</p><p>1151 Chapel Street</p><p>New Haven, CT 06511</p><p>Phone: +1-833-GRADHOTELS</p><p>Estimated price/night: $250-$350</p><p>Website: <a href="https://www.hilton.com/en/hotels/hvngngu-graduate-new-haven/" title="https://www.hilton.com/en/hotels/hvngngu-graduate-new-haven/" data-msys-clicktrack="0" target="_blank" rel="ugc nofollow noopener noreferrer">https://www.hilton.com/en/hotels/hvngngu-graduate-new-haven/</a></p><p><br></p><p>The Blake Hotel</p><p>9 High Street<br>New Haven, CT 06510<br>Phone: 203-390-5352</p><p>Estimated price/night: $250-$300</p><p>Website: <a href="https://theblakenewhaven.com/" title="https://theblakenewhaven.com/" data-msys-clicktrack="0" target="_blank" rel="ugc nofollow noopener noreferrer">https://theblakenewhaven.com/</a></p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Travel Stipends</strong></strong></p><p>The English Institute is pleased to offer travel stipends of $300 each to graduate students and contingent faculty attending the conference. These awards are in addition to the $300 stipends available to one graduate student or faculty member from each sponsoring institution. Graduate students and contingent faculty interested in applying should email their application, a short letter of intent and estimated budget, to <a href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/the-english-institute-82nd-annual-meeting-registration-1407757413319?aff=oddtdtcreator" title="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/the-english-institute-82nd-annual-meeting-registration-1407757413319?aff=oddtdtcreator" data-msys-clicktrack="0" target="_blank" rel="ugc nofollow noopener noreferrer"><strong><strong>englishinstitute@yale.edu</strong></strong></a>. The conference organizers will review applications, and funding decisions will be communicated directly to applicants.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Registration</strong></strong></p><p>Faculty &amp; Students from Sponsoring Institutions: FREE</p><p>Faculty from Non-Sponsoring Institutions: $50</p><p>Students &amp; Scholars from Non-Sponsoring Institutions: $20</p><p>We request that all conference attendees fill out the online registration form (name, institutional affiliation, email address) as soon as you can, since room capacity is limited.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Membership</strong></strong></p><p>For an <strong><strong>annual donation of $600,</strong></strong><strong><strong> </strong></strong><a href="https://englishinstitute.yale.edu/institutional-sponsors-1" title="https://englishinstitute.yale.edu/institutional-sponsors-1" data-msys-clicktrack="0" target="_blank" rel="ugc nofollow noopener noreferrer"><strong><strong>sponsoring institutions</strong></strong></a><strong><strong> </strong></strong><strong><strong>enjoy a waived registration fee for all faculty and students,</strong></strong> a listing in all promotional materials, and participation in The English Institute's travel subsidy program, which provides up to $250 toward transportation and lodging costs for one graduate student or one untenured faculty participant.</p><p>To become a sponsor, please contact <a href="https://englishinstitute.yale.edu/" title="https://englishinstitute.yale.edu/" data-msys-clicktrack="0" target="_blank" rel="ugc nofollow noopener noreferrer">The English Institute </a>at englishinstitute@yale.edu.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Questions?</strong></strong> Contact The English Institute at englishinstitute@yale.edu or visit <a href="http://englishinstitute.yale.edu/" title="http://englishinstitute.yale.edu/" data-msys-clicktrack="0" target="_blank" rel="ugc nofollow noopener noreferrer">http://englishinstitute.yale.edu</a> for further information.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p></div></div><div class="Overview-module-scss-module__dJyb9a__fadeOut"></div></div><button class="Overview-module-scss-module__dJyb9a__readMore" type="button" data-heap-id="Listings - Description - Read more - Click" aria-label="Read more about this event">Read more</button></div><div class="Divider-module-scss-module__AzJCpq__divider"></div><div class="SectionWrapper-module-scss-module__5yIgma__section" data-testid="section-wrapper-goodToKnow"><div class="GoodToKnow-module-scss-module__SccLQq__g2k"><div class="GoodToKnow_goodToKnow__ramez"><div class="Layout_wrapper__zapcr"><div class="Layout_headWrapper__zapcr"><h2 class="Layout_title__zapcr">Good to know</h2></div><div class="Layout_itemList__zapcr"><div style="margin:0;padding:0"></div><div class="Card_card--stretched__ddcdt" data-testid="card"><div class="Card_contentWrapper__ddcdt"><p class="Card_title__ddcdt">Highlights</p><div class="Card_body__ddcdt Highlights_body__1djuo"><ul class="Highlights_wrapper__1djuo"><li class="Highlights_highlightItem__1djuo"><i class="Icon_root__1qs3z Icon_icon-xsmall__1qs3z" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none"><path d="M0.667969 7.99996C0.667969 3.94987 3.95121 0.666626 8.0013 0.666626C8.7419 0.666626 9.45685 0.776409 10.1308 0.98059L9.74417 2.25664C9.19423 2.09003 8.60949 1.99996 8.0013 1.99996C4.68759 1.99996 2.0013 4.68625 2.0013 7.99996C2.0013 11.3137 4.68759 14 8.0013 14C8.60949 14 9.19423 13.9099 9.74417 13.7433L10.1308 15.0193C9.45685 15.2235 8.7419 15.3333 8.0013 15.3333C3.95121 15.3333 0.667969 12.05 0.667969 7.99996Z" fill="#261B36"></path><path d="M15.0207 10.1294C15.2249 9.45551 15.3346 8.74055 15.3346 7.99996C15.3346 7.25936 15.2249 6.54441 15.0207 5.87048L13.7446 6.25709C13.9112 6.80703 14.0013 7.39177 14.0013 7.99996C14.0013 8.60814 13.9112 9.19288 13.7446 9.74283L