location_text":"New Haven, Connecticut"}},"trackingAction":"BreadcrumbAddress","trackingCategory":"listing"},{"link":"/d/ct--new-haven/seminar","text":{"text":"{relevant_place_name} {format_string}","isLocalized":true,"placeholders":{"format_string":"seminars","relevant_place_name":"New Haven"}},"trackingAction":"BreadcrumbFormat","trackingCategory":"listing"},{"link":"/d/ct--new-haven/business--seminar","text":{"text":"{relevant_place_name} {category_string} {format_string}","isLocalized":true,"placeholders":{"category_string":"Business","format_string":"seminars","relevant_place_name":"New Haven"}},"trackingAction":"BreadcrumbCategory","trackingCategory":"listing"}],"performers":{"headliners":[],"supporters":[]},"taxonomies":{"category":"Business","subcategory":"Educators","format":"Seminar"},"artistInfo":null,"presenterInfo":{"presenter":null},"structuredContent":{"modules":[{"type":"text","text":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe 83rd Annual English Institute meeting, \"Reversal,\" will take place October 2-3, 2026 at Yale University. This event is co-sponsored by the Whitney Humanities Center.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor more than seven decades, The English Institute has been a major resource for developments in criticism, theory, and scholarship, while honoring traditional fields of interest and modes of literary analysis.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThree institutions will now host The English Institute conference: Yale University (2015, 2018, 2023, and 2026), the University of Chicago (2016, 2019, 2024), and the University of California at Irvine (2017, 2022, and 2025).\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eShared reading for \"The Conversation\": Friedrich Nietzsche, \"On Truth and Lying in a Non-Moral Sense\" (\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-uyPEl4uvHumCePUWbGiAMyZP9UmE9Mh/view?usp=drive_link\" title=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-uyPEl4uvHumCePUWbGiAMyZP9UmE9Mh/view?usp=drive_link\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003elinked here\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e).\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSchedule\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFriday, October 2\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e1:00 pm\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Welcome\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e1:10 pm\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Welcome (Yoon Sun Lee and Daniel Stout)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e1:20 pm\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Bonnie Honig, “The Accidental Ordinary: Euripides' \u003cem\u003e\u003cem\u003eHippolytus\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/em\u003e in Reverse” (Introduced by Jennifer Fleissner)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e2:50 pm\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Coffee break\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e3:00 pm\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Sarah Beckwith, “The Impossibility of Reversal: Shakespeare’s Turnings in \u003cem\u003e\u003cem\u003eThe Winter’s Tale\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/em\u003e and Some Intertexts” (Introduced by Nancy Yousef)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e4:30 pm\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Coffee break\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e5:00 pm\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Emily Greenwood, “Third Person Regret: Shipwreck and Black Atlantic Counterfactuals” (Introduced by Kevin Quashie)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e6:30 pm:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e Opening Reception\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSaturday, October 3\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e8:30 am\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Continental breakfast\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e9:00 am\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Heather Love, “Doubling Back” (Introduced by Caleb Smith)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e10:45 am\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Coffee break\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e11:00am\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Daniel Hack, “Expectations? Great!” (Introduced by Virginia Jackson)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e12:45 pm\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Lunch\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e1:45 pm\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: The Conversation: Friedrich Nietzsche, “On Truth and Lying in a Non-Moral Sense”\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e2:45 pm\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Coffee break\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e3:00 pm\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Minou Arjomand, “Aesthetic Labor from Wagner to Abortion Theater” (Introduced by Shonni Enelow)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e4:45 pm\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Mel Y. Chen, “Method’s Negative Spaces” (Introduced by Meredith Martin)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e6:15 pm\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: Closing reception\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTravel\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDepending on where you are coming from, there are several ways to travel into New Haven.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eAir\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.aveloair.com/\" title=\"https://www.aveloair.com/\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003eAvelo Airlines\u003c/a\u003e flies to Tweed New Haven Airport (HVN) from twenty-six locations. Yale campus is a 10-15 minute car ride from the airport.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePlease note that most major (New York area) airports are between two and five hours from New Haven via shuttle bus, train, or car. It is best to plan to arrive at these airports in the early morning to early afternoon.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you will be flying, we recommend flying into La Guardia International Airport. From there you will take a shuttle bus to Grand Central Station and take the Metro North to New Haven's Union Station. The Metro North runs regularly and does not require purchasing tickets before arriving at the train station. Another excellent option is flying into Newark airport. From Newark you can take an Amtrak train to New Haven's Union Station. While Amtrak prices fluctuate you are able to book in advance and reserve seats.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eGround\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you are travelling regionally and would like to take the train to New Haven you can take the Metro North from New York City's Grand Central Station to New Haven's Union Station or the Amtrak can be taken from most major hubs to New Haven's Union Station.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href=\"https://your.yale.edu/campus-essentials/getting-around-campus/using-the-shuttle\" title=\"https://your.yale.edu/campus-essentials/getting-around-campus/using-the-shuttle\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003eYale Shuttle\u003c/a\u003e provides service between Union Station and campus destinations. Please note that there are now TWO shuttle stop locations in front of Union Station. If the stop directly in front of the station is congested, shuttle drivers pick up in front of the parking garage. Please look for Shuttles in both locations.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTaxis meet all trains and buses at Union Station in New Haven. Include a tip for taxi drivers of about 15% of the total fare; add an extra $1 to $2 for help with luggage. Uber and Lyft are also widely available in New Haven.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHotels near the conference include\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Study at Yale\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1157 Chapel Street\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNew Haven, CT 06511\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePhone: 203.503.3900\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEstimated price/night: $250-$300\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWebsite: \u003ca href=\"https://www.thestudyatyale.com/\" title=\"https://www.thestudyatyale.com/\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttps://www.thestudyatyale.com/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNew Haven Hotel\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e229 George Street\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNew Haven, CT 06510\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePhone: 203-498-3100\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEstimated price/night: $174-$274\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWebsite: \u003ca href=\"https://www.newhavenhotel.com/?gad_source=1\u0026amp;gclid=Cj0KCQiAoeGuBhCBARIsAGfKY7zHF28iwfAr8B3Ma6UAPlSZDHwJhcyFZrp666sFXXsa5gbYq3na_oUaAk1QEALw_wcB\" title=\"https://www.newhavenhotel.com/?gad_source=1\u0026amp;gclid=Cj0KCQiAoeGuBhCBARIsAGfKY7zHF28iwfAr8B3Ma6UAPlSZDHwJhcyFZrp666sFXXsa5gbYq3na_oUaAk1QEALw_wcB\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttps://www.newhavenhotel.com/?gad_source=1\u0026amp;gclid=Cj0KCQiAoeGuBhCBARIsAGfKY7zHF28iwfAr8B3Ma6UAPlSZDHwJhcyFZrp666sFXXsa5gbYq3na_oUaAk1QEALw_wcB\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eOMNI New Haven at Yale\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e155 Temple Street\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNew Haven, CT 06510\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePhone: 203-772-6664\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEstimated price/night: $150-$250\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWebsite: \u003ca href=\"https://www.omnihotels.com/hotels/new-haven-yale?_gl=1*a6pt1v*_gcl_au*MTE3ODYzNzg2MS4xNzc4NTM3MzIz*_ga*MTU4MjYzNjM1MC4xNzc4NTM3MzI0*_ga_BELGX2HEXN*czE3Nzg1MzczMjMkbzEkZzEkdDE3Nzg1MzgxMTAkajI2JGwwJGgw\" title=\"https://www.omnihotels.com/hotels/new-haven-yale?_gl=1*a6pt1v*_gcl_au*MTE3ODYzNzg2MS4xNzc4NTM3MzIz*_ga*MTU4MjYzNjM1MC4xNzc4NTM3MzI0*_ga_BELGX2HEXN*czE3Nzg1MzczMjMkbzEkZzEkdDE3Nzg1MzgxMTAkajI2JGwwJGgw\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttps://www.omnihotels.com/hotels/new-haven-yale?_gl=1*a6pt1v*_gcl_au*MTE3ODYzNzg2MS4xNzc4NTM3MzIz*_ga*MTU4MjYzNjM1MC4xNzc4NTM3MzI0*_ga_BELGX2HEXN*czE3Nzg1MzczMjMkbzEkZzEkdDE3Nzg1MzgxMTAkajI2JGwwJGgw\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Graduate by Hilton New Haven\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1151 Chapel Street\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNew Haven, CT 06511\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePhone: +1-833-GRADHOTELS\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEstimated price/night: $250-$350\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWebsite: \u003ca href=\"https://www.hilton.com/en/hotels/hvngngu-graduate-new-haven/\" title=\"https://www.hilton.com/en/hotels/hvngngu-graduate-new-haven/\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttps://www.hilton.com/en/hotels/hvngngu-graduate-new-haven/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Blake Hotel\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e9 High Street\u003cbr\u003eNew Haven, CT 06510\u003cbr\u003ePhone: 203-390-5352\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEstimated price/night: $250-$300\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWebsite: \u003ca href=\"https://theblakenewhaven.com/\" title=\"https://theblakenewhaven.com/\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttps://theblakenewhaven.com/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTravel Stipends\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe English Institute is pleased to offer travel stipends of $300 each to graduate students and contingent faculty attending the conference. These awards are in addition to the $300 stipends available to one graduate student or faculty member from each sponsoring institution. Graduate students and contingent faculty interested in applying should email their application, a short letter of intent and estimated budget, to \u003ca href=\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/the-english-institute-82nd-annual-meeting-registration-1407757413319?aff=oddtdtcreator\" title=\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/the-english-institute-82nd-annual-meeting-registration-1407757413319?aff=oddtdtcreator\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eenglishinstitute@yale.edu\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. The conference organizers will review applications, and funding decisions will be communicated directly to applicants.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRegistration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFaculty \u0026amp; Students from Sponsoring Institutions: FREE\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFaculty from Non-Sponsoring Institutions: $50\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eStudents \u0026amp; Scholars from Non-Sponsoring Institutions: $20\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe request that all conference attendees fill out the online registration form (name, institutional affiliation, email address) as soon as you can, since room capacity is limited.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMembership\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor an \u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eannual donation of $600,\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e \u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://englishinstitute.yale.edu/institutional-sponsors-1\" title=\"https://englishinstitute.yale.edu/institutional-sponsors-1\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003esponsoring institutions\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e \u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eenjoy a waived registration fee for all faculty and students,\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e a listing in all promotional materials, and participation in The English Institute's travel subsidy program, which provides up to $250 toward transportation and lodging costs for one graduate student or one untenured faculty participant.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo become a sponsor, please contact \u003ca href=\"https://englishinstitute.yale.edu/\" title=\"https://englishinstitute.yale.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003eThe English Institute \u003c/a\u003eat englishinstitute@yale.edu.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eQuestions?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e Contact The English Institute at englishinstitute@yale.edu or visit \u003ca href=\"http://englishinstitute.yale.edu/\" title=\"http://englishinstitute.yale.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttp://englishinstitute.yale.edu\u003c/a\u003e for further information.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003