<div class="inner"><div class="jsx-5b96bbb25927e633"><div class="jsx-5b96bbb25927e633 flex-column content"><div class="jsx-4fc9988e16909c6d message">Welcome! To join the event, please register below. </div><div class="jsx-5b96bbb25927e633 mt-1 flex-column content"><div class="jsx-5b96bbb25927e633 cta-wrapper"><div class="jsx-5b96bbb25927e633 cta flex-center gap-2 mb-1"><button class="btn lux-button flex-center medium primary solid variant-color-primary full-width no-icon" type="button"><div class="label">Register</div></button></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="jsx-5981e6e33e2304d4 content-card pb-1 event-about-card"><div class="jsx-5981e6e33e2304d4 card-title flex-center gap-2 spread"><div class="jsx-5981e6e33e2304d4 title-label text-tinted fs-sm">About Event</div></div><div class="jsx-5981e6e33e2304d4 content"><div class="spark-content" dir="auto"><p class="">​<!-- -->In this lunch-and-learn panel, three advanced student founders will share how they approach the practice of identification in innovation, from defining purpose and intended impact to identifying initial users, audiences, customers, and partners.</p><p class="">​<!-- -->The conversation will offer a practical look at how student founders are working through these foundational questions as their ventures develop. Attendees will also have the opportunity to ask questions, hear directly from peers navigating the founder journey, and learn from the decisions shaping their work.</p><p class="">​<!-- -->All Tsai CITY Venture Development Program participants and others interested in student founders&#x27; work are welcome.</p></div></div></div><div class="jsx-5981e6e33e2304d4 content-card"><div class="jsx-5981e6e33e2304d4 card-title flex-center gap-2 spread"><div class="jsx-5981e6e33e2304d4 title-label text-tinted fs-sm">Location</div></div><div class="jsx-5981e6e33e2304d4 content"><div class="jsx-bc498e5f7dced08b info"><div class="cursor-copy jsx-bc498e5f7dced08b"><div class="jsx-bc498e5f