+          <div class="Article-blocks"><div class="Text Text--small Text--space-m-bottom-medium Text--space-d-bottom-medium">
+  <div class="Text-inner"><p>Start your day energized! Join us for complimentary coffee and treats from 10:00-10:30 AM, setting the stage for an engaging and informal conversation with 2026 Windham-Campbell Prize recipients <a href="/@/page/l28vbimva4i1dt6f" target="_blank">Kei Miller,</a> <a href="/@/page/ggufu9m2keq1pxos" target="_blank">Gwendoline Riley</a>, <a href="/@/page/ecxge6c84j1ythdp" target="_blank">Adam Ehrlich Sachs</a>, <a href="/@/page/lbbesfehgnehfvgi" target="_blank">Lucy Sante</a>, and James Surowiecki, senior editor at <em>The Yale Review</em>, offering a unique opportunity to connect directly with some of today’s most compelling literary voices in a relaxed setting.</p></div>
+</div>
+<hr class="Line" />
+<div class="Text Text--small Text--space-m-bottom-medium Text--space-d-bottom-medium">
+  <div class="Text-inner"><p>James Surowiecki is an editor at <em>The Yale Review</em>, journalist, and author. He’s the author of the national bestseller <em>The Wisdom of Crowds</em> (2004), and a contributing writer to <em>The Atlantic</em>. He was a columnist at <em>The New Yorker</em> for 17 years, writing the popular bi-weekly business column “The Financial Page.” He also wrote the <em>Bottom Line</em> column for <em>New York</em> magazine and was a business columnist for <em>Slate</em>. His writing has appeared in a wide range of publications, including, among others, <em>The New York Times Magazine, The Wall Street Journal, Wired</em>, and <em>The New York Review of Books</em>. Surowiecki has also worked in documentary film and television. He was senior story producer and writer for the HBO series Vice News Tonight, and co-produced and wrote two films on the history and meaning of college football for ESPN.</p></div>
+</div>
